Recorded answers from `lpstat -p`, `lpstat -d` and `lpinfo -v`; `lpstat -r` is
read too, and a file that is not here reads as an empty answer.

A surface whose picture depends on three programs on the host's PATH cannot be
goldened: a machine with CUPS set up and one without draw different frames and
neither is wrong. `kdos-print --fixture testing/fixtures/print` reads these
instead of running them.

The `serial`, `file` and bare `network socket` rows are here ON PURPOSE.
`lpinfo -v` lists every backend CUPS has, including one that prints to a file,
one that names a serial port with nothing on it, and each backend that found no
device by itself, as a scheme with no address; offering any of them as a printer
to add is offering a queue that will never produce a page. The golden is what
proves they are dropped.
